  "notes": "USAGE: {洞察|どうさつ} implies seeing beyond the surface to understand underlying truths. Often used with {力|りょく} to form {洞察力|どうさつりょく} (insight, perceptiveness).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {洞察力|どうさつりょく} (insight, perceptiveness)\n- {鋭|するど}い{洞察|どうさつ} (keen/sharp insight)\n- {深|ふか}い{洞察|どうさつ} (deep insight)\n- {洞察|どうさつ}を{得|え}る (to gain insight)\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {観察|かんさつ} (observation - more external, empirical)\n- {察知|さっち} (perception - detecting/sensing)\n- {見抜|みぬ}く (to see through - verb form)",
